      "writtenOn": "2020-08-13T07:43:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function should only be used when errors are not expected, usually because it\u0027s just parsing something that was previously serialized to a property struct. Switching to one of those error handling methods makes this function more or less the same as the other, since the caller is responsible for checking for and handling the error case (I believe those error functions don\u0027t actually interrupt soong immediately, so we\u0027d have to return nil and the caller would need to handle that).",
